-- SHADOW-SEMANTICS cell D25 (S2 definer arm, RETURN-POSITION, matrix row 39 / #1430): this
-- module DEFINES its own `zed : Int` AND imports `Zed` BY NAME, so the interface is
-- unambiguously nameable here and `zed` IS a definer shadow. S2's inversion is
-- unconditional -- the impl universe is not consulted -- so the module's own binding
-- answers: 42 + 0 = 42, on every verb.
--
-- 🚨 D25 IS THE DISCRIMINATING TWIN OF D24, AND THE CORPUS HAD ONLY THE D24 SIDE.
-- d24_definer_return_pos_not_nameable and i21_importer_return_pos_not_nameable are the
-- only two return-position cells in this corpus, and BOTH are NOT-NAMEABLE: they pass
-- because S1 DECLINES TO CLASSIFY, so neither of them ever reaches S2's inversion at all.
-- The nameable cell -- the one that does reach it -- had no fixture here; it lived only
-- as a self-draining must-fail pin, which this gate cannot see. Row 39 states the
-- consequence directly: "This is why row 38 must not be read as covering return position".
--
-- MEASURED AT THE PARENT COMMIT, MEDAKA_STRICT=1, every command redirected to a file with
-- $? read separately: `check` exit 0 with zero diagnostics, `run` exit 0 printing **777**
-- (the impl body -- the S0 half, a wrong value with no diagnostic on any verb before it),
-- `build` exit 1 with `runtime error [E-PANIC]: unbound method: zed`. Three verbs, three
-- answers. All three now answer 42, which is why this cell is graded ALL_EXACT rather than
-- on an ACCEPT/REJECT column: every column was already ACCEPT on the `check` arm while the
-- value was wrong, so a status-only assertion could not have seen this.
--
-- 🚨 DO NOT "SIMPLIFY" `zed : a` INTO A METHOD WITH AN ARGUMENT. The load-bearing axis is
-- RETURN-POSITION-NESS, not the nameability that rows 33-38 vary. Give the method an
-- argument mentioning the typaram and the inversion already fired correctly before this
-- fix -- the cell would then be green vacuously and pin nothing. Likewise keep `sf` in the
-- import list: it is what puts `smod` in the module graph at all.
import smod.{Zed, sf}

zed : Int
zed = 42

main = println (zed + sf 0)
